{
 "page": "DinosaurPlanet.html",
 "header": [
  "The page's plan for N64Recomp-browser's tools/play_page.mjs: the launcher, Load ROM on a new profile once the shader",
  "list Chrome builds behind it is done (Firefox builds none there and says so), Start Game, the logos, then the game",
  "select and a New Game as a player makes one, with the keyboard's defaults (Space is A, Enter Start, WASD the stick):",
  "A on the first file (once the report says the game select, menu 5), A for an A in the name, the stick to END, each",
  "a tap of one game frame, since the name screen moves its cursor a letter a frame while the stick is held, and A on the",
  "new file until the game leaves the game select. The opening plays as a new game's does, the",
  "pterodactyl and the storm, until the report puts Krystal in a map (tools/survey.js's playing()), and she walks",
  "about there. Then the plan starts areas from story points as the desktop build's tests do (survey.js's go(), each a",
  "need that fails the run unless the game puts the player in that map), with the object groups docs/story-points.md",
  "names where it names them, since a story point leaves a map's enemies and props off:",
  "SwapStone Hollow (warp 15, its Queen, Tricky and mushrooms on) for 30 s with the pause menu opened and closed, and",
  "Cape Claw at the sand worm's fight (before-sand-worm) for 20 s. About 2.5 minutes. tools/play_plan_extended.json",
  "goes on to five more areas, for when a longer play is needed.",
  "Its waits and holds are on the game's own clock (survey.js's clock(), 60 a second), but for the pause menu's, since",
  "that clock stands still while the game is paused."
 ],
